<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">King George Sound</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King George Sound is a large natural harbour on the south coast of Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, on which the town of Albany stands. George Vancouver named it in 1791, and in 1826 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> set up a military garrison there to forestall French claims, the first European settlement in Western Australia. It later became a coaling port and an assembly point for Australian troops sailing to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-george-sound.jpg" alt="King George Sound" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hughesdarren · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_King_George_Sound_drawn_using_Paint.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
